                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/14306: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-08-26T19:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1941—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>149. Your 311, August 24, noon. Please keep Department promptly informed on
                    Turkish reaction to Anglo-Russian invasion of Iran, and what effect, if any,
                    this is likely to have on Turkey’s future attitude toward Britain and the
                    Axis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
